## 3️⃣ ALGORITHM PATTERNS

### Use optimal patterns:

| Problem Type | Pattern | Complexity |
|-------------|---------|------------|
| Find pair with sum | Two pointers / Hash | O(n) |
| Sliding window | Deque / Two pointers | O(n) |
| Top K elements | Heap | O(n log k) |
| Graph traversal | BFS/DFS | O(V + E) |
| Shortest path | Dijkstra / BFS | O(E log V) |
| Range sum/update | Prefix sum / Segment tree | O(1) / O(log n) |
| String matching | KMP / Rabin-Karp | O(n + m) |
| Subset/combination | Bit manipulation | O(2^n) |

❌ Forbidden:
```python
# O(n²) - Nested loops for pair finding
def find_pair_with_sum(nums, target):
    for i, a in enumerate(nums):
        for j, b in enumerate(nums[i+1:], i+1):
            if a + b == target:
                return (i, j)
```

✅ Required:
```python
# O(n) - Hash map approach
def find_pair_with_sum(nums: list[int], target: int) -> tuple[int, int] | None:
    seen: dict[int, int] = {}
    for i, num in enumerate(nums):
        complement = target - num
        if complement in seen:
            return (seen[complement], i)
        seen[num] = i
    return None
```

