## 4️⃣ DATABASE QUERY EFFICIENCY

### Index Usage
- ALWAYS check if query uses index
- Composite indexes for multi-column filters
- Covering indexes for read-heavy queries

### Query Optimization
❌ Forbidden:
```python
# N+1 problem - O(n) queries
users = await session.execute(select(User))
for user in users.scalars():
    print(user.role.name)  # Additional query per user
```

✅ Required:
```python
# O(1) queries - eager loading
stmt = select(User).options(joinedload(User.role))
users = await session.execute(stmt)
for user in users.scalars():
    print(user.role.name)  # No additional query
```

### Pagination
❌ Forbidden:
```python
# Offset pagination - O(n) for deep pages
select(User).offset(10000).limit(10)
```

✅ Required:
```python
# Cursor pagination - O(1) for any page
select(User).where(User.id > last_seen_id).limit(10)
```

